&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The results weren&amp;rsquo;t great though &amp;ndash; many nav elements and alignments were off.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BSIE [Bootstrap IE]
&lt;a class="link" href="http://www.bootcss.com/p/bsie/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;http://www.bootcss.com/p/bsie/&lt;/a&gt;
This is an open-source library built on top of Bootstrap. The demo looked great, but due to legacy reasons, my site was already built and making changes was too difficult, so I had to give up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The final solution: just embed two JS files.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="html5shivjs--respondjs"&gt;html5shiv.js + respond.js
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Yes, just these two JS files. At least IE7 and above now display properly. There are still some minor issues like rounded corners, but the nav, grid layout, and overall appearance work well. Very satisfying.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
